Package: ggchord
Title: Multi-Sequence Alignment Chord Diagram Visualization Tool
Version: 0.14.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Jem", family = "Dang", email = "dangjem0730@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A 'ggplot2'-based package for multi-sequence alignment chord
    diagrams, linear collinearity plots and single circular sequence maps.
    A layered grammar combines
    sequence backbones, interval links, genes, general biological features,
    labels, genomic axes and restriction sites. Feature placement is expressed
    with composable Position objects, while role-specific scales and themes
    keep data mapping separate from geometry and appearance.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: ggplot2 (>= 4.0.0), grDevices, grid, rlang, scales
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown, qpdf, dplyr, svglite, testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    readxl, digest, GenomicRanges, InteractionSet, IRanges, S4Vectors
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
URL: https://github.com/DangJem/ggchord, https://dangjem.github.io/ggchord/
BugReports: https://github.com/DangJem/ggchord/issues
NeedsCompilation: no
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
